 "_sources": {
  "long_term": "MillGNN (Wu et al., CIKM 2025, arXiv:2509.03852) Table 2: input 96, MSE / MAE; MillGNN tuned with NNI (20 trials); other rows as cited or re-run (*) by MillGNN. MoVE: ICLR 2026 submission, Table 4 (input 96, seed 2024; no Exchange). LagTS: Liu et al., ICASSP 2025, Table I (input 96; evaluated on ETTh1, ETTh2, Exchange and Weather only; lambda tuned in {0.05, 0.1, 0.15, 0.2}). S-Mamba and TimesNet: Wang et al., \"Is Mamba Effective for Time Series Forecasting?\", Neurocomputing 2025 (arXiv:2403.11144), Tables 2-4 (input 96); its iTransformer, PatchTST and DLinear columns agree with the numbers above.",
  "pems": "MillGNN Table 3 (TimeMixer protocol: input 96, horizon 12, MAE / MAPE in % / RMSE on the original scale).",
  "pems_96": "PEMS03/04/07/08, input 96, horizons 12/24/48/96, MSE / MAE on the normalised scale (protocol of iTransformer): iTransformer, PatchTST, DLinear and TimesNet from the iTransformer paper (ICLR 2024), Table 9; S-Mamba from Wang et al. (Neurocomputing 2025), Table 2.",
  "solar": "Solar-Energy (long_term / Solar), input 96: S-Mamba, iTransformer, PatchTST, DLinear and TimesNet from Wang et al. (S-Mamba, Neurocomputing 2025), Table 4.",
  "informer_timexer": "long_term / Informer, input 96: TimesNet (Wu et al., ICLR 2023) Table 13 for ETTh1, ETTh2 (horizon 96 only), ETTm1, ETTm2; Autoformer (Wu et al., NeurIPS 2021) Table 1 for Electricity, Exchange, Traffic, Weather. long_term / TimeXer, look-back 96: TimeXer (Wang et al., NeurIPS 2024), full multivariate results for ETTh1, ETTh2, Weather, Electricity; Table 3 averages (key Avg) for ETTm1, ETTm2, Traffic.",
  "smamba_paper": "The reference of the baseline check: Wang et al., \"Is Mamba Effective for Time Series Forecasting?\", Neurocomputing 2025 (arXiv:2403.11144, HTML version of v3), Tables 2-4: input 96, horizons 96/192/336/720 (PEMS: 12/24/48/96), MSE / MAE on the normalised scale, for S-Mamba, iTransformer, RLinear, PatchTST, DLinear and TiDE on all 13 datasets. The baseline columns equal the iTransformer paper (ICLR 2024, Tables 8-9), whose Appendix A.2 states that the baselines were reproduced in the TimesNet benchmark (Time-Series-Library) with the configurations of each model's paper or official code."
